abstract: >
  Tamarin prover theories and automation scripts for the formal verification of
  security properties of a four-pool BPMN procurement collaboration under
  multiple platform enforcement profiles (loose coupling, smart-contract
  orchestration, Verifiable Credential–based self-orchestration, full
  Dolev-Yao). The artifact reproduces 20 verification configurations and six
  security lemmas (G1, G2, G3, G4, G7, G6a), and isolates a
  time-of-check-to-time-of-use behaviour under non-atomic Verifiable Data
  Registry semantics.
